@model DownstreamModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Downstream API";
}

<h1>Calling an API with the user's token</h1>
<p class="sub">
    The provider's UserInfo endpoint stands in for a protected API here, but the calling pattern is
    the one to copy.
</p>

<div class="card">
    <pre>var request = new HttpRequestMessage(HttpMethod.Get, endpoint);
await request.WithArkTokenAsync(HttpContext);   // attaches the current access token

using var response = await httpClient.SendAsync(request);</pre>
    <div class="note">
        <code>WithArkTokenAsync</code> reads the token from the authentication cookie at call time,
        which matters: the cookie handler may have refreshed it since the page began rendering.
        Capturing the token into a field or a static client is the usual cause of a call that
        works for an hour and then starts returning 401.
    </div>
</div>

<h2>Result</h2>
<div class="card">
    <div class="kv">
        <div>Endpoint</div><div><code>@Model.Endpoint</code></div>
        <div>Status</div>
        <div>
            @if (Model.Error != null)
            {
                <span class="pill bad">failed</span>
            }
            else if (Model.StatusCode is >= 200 and < 300)
            {
                <span class="pill ok">@Model.StatusCode</span>
            }
            else
            {
                <span class="pill warn">@Model.StatusCode</span>
            }
        </div>
    </div>

    @if (Model.Error != null)
    {
        <div class="note bad">@Model.Error</div>
    }
    else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Model.Body))
    {
        <div style="margin-top:12px"><pre>@Model.Body</pre></div>
    }
</div>

<h2>Protecting an API of your own</h2>
<div class="card">
    <p style="margin-top:0">
        The receiving side is the mirror image — validate the bearer token against the same
        provider, with signing keys taken from its JWKS document rather than a configured public
        key:
    </p>
    <pre>builder.Services
    .AddAuthentication()
    .AddArkOidcApi(arkConfig);   // JWT bearer, keys discovered from {Authority}/.well-known/jwks.json</pre>
    <div class="note">
        Set <code>Audience</code> in the API's own <code>ark_oauth_client</code> section so a token
        minted for a different application cannot be replayed against it.
    </div>
</div>
